-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The data files contain identifiers and derived counts drawn from external
sources, which remain subject to their own terms:

  - Adverse-event report counts are derived from the openFDA FAERS API, a
    public data service of the United States Food and Drug Administration.
  - RxNorm concept identifiers (rxcui_a, rxcui_b) originate from the U.S.
    National Library of Medicine.
  - ATC codes (atc_a, atc_b) are used for classification; ATC is maintained by
    the WHO Collaborating Centre for Drug Statistics Methodology.
  - DrugBank identifiers (drugbank_a, drugbank_b) are cross-references to
    DrugBank, which applies its own licence to its content. Only the accession
    strings are reproduced here.
  - ChEMBL identifiers (chembl_a, chembl_b) are cross-references to ChEMBL
    (EMBL-EBI).

No third-party database content is redistributed beyond the identifier strings
and the aggregate counts described in data/DATA_DICTIONARY.md.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO CLINICAL WARRANTY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This release is an evaluation and benchmarking resource. It does not license
the co-prescription of any drug pair and is not a source of clinical
drug-interaction information. Nothing in it substitutes for the judgement of a
qualified healthcare professional with access to the full patient context and a
current, maintained drug-information source. The licences above grant rights to
use and redistribute these materials; they grant no warranty of clinical
fitness of any kind.
